# School ERP — Core Architecture

**Stack:** Java 17, Spring Boot 3+, Spring Security, JWT, Redis, OTP, MySQL, JPA/Hibernate, Flyway, Maven, REST only (no WebSocket, no GraphQL).

**Base package:** `com.schoolerp`

## Architecture

- Modular monolith, feature-based modules, layered design
- Constructor injection only (no field injection)
- Lombok, SOLID, clean architecture
- No wildcard imports; no hardcoded strings (use `constants/`)

## Project Layout

```
src/main/java/com/schoolerp/
├── config/ common/ constants/ exception/ security/ util/ scheduler/
└── modules/
    ├── auth/ student/ parent/ staff/ attendance/ admission/ academic/
    ├── billing/ invoice/ payment/ scholarship/ communication/
    ├── notification/ reports/ uploads/ settings/ transfercertificate/
```

## Module Layout (every module)

```
controller/ service/ service/impl/ repository/ entity/
dto/request/ dto/response/ mapper/ validator/ enums/
```

**communication/** also: `provider/`, `template/`, `scheduler/` (under module).

## Shared Packages

| Package | Contents |
|---------|----------|
| `common/` | BaseEntity, ApiResponse, ErrorResponse, PaginationResponse, audit |
| `constants/` | ApiConstants, SecurityConstants, MessageConstants, RedisConstants |
| `exception/` | GlobalExceptionHandler, BusinessException, UnauthorizedException, ValidationException, ResourceNotFoundException |
| `security/` | jwt/, filter/, config/, service/ |
| `util/` | DateUtil, JwtUtil, OtpUtil, FileUtil, CommonUtil |
| `scheduler/` | FeeReminderScheduler, NotificationScheduler |

## Generation Policy (critical)

**Do NOT auto-generate** unless the developer explicitly requests:

- APIs, controllers, services, repositories, entities

**Default focus:** structure, architecture, standards, reusable patterns, scalability.

When implementing a requested feature, still follow module layout and shared packages above.
